// WHY: `@std.avrac` library entry — exposes the Avra compiler as a
// reusable library so downstream tools (the `avra` CLI binary,
// editor plugins, doc generators, fuzz harnesses) can invoke any
// pipeline stage without pulling in a CLI driver.
//
// All public symbols are accessible by their submodule path, e.g.
// `use @std.avrac.parse.{parse_program_source}`,
// `use @std.avrac.codegen.{compile_program}`,
// `use @std.avrac.diagnostics.{bag_has_errors}`.
//
// The bootstrap module resolver wraps this file's contents in
// `Module("@std") { Module("avrac") { ... } }` so every submodule
// declared below becomes addressable at `@std.avrac.<sub>`.

mod core
mod diagnostics
mod parse
mod features
mod typeck
mod resolve
mod codegen
mod desugar
mod render
mod pathutil
mod coverage
mod indexer
mod docs
mod lang_gen
mod fmt
mod test_runner
mod build
